+### Formulas
+- Optical depth increment: $pcnt = ray.world\_step \times \sigma$ [S3, unofficial].
+- Sample weight: $weight = \exp(log\_transmit) \times (1 - \exp(-pcnt))$ [S3, unofficial].
+- Log-transmittance update: $log\_transmit \leftarrow log\_transmit - pcnt$ [S3, unofficial].
+- Color accumulation: $outv \leftarrow outv + weight \times \max(lane\_color\_total + 0.5, 0.0)$ [S3, unofficial].
+- Early termination condition: $\exp(log\_transmit) < opt.stop\_thresh$ [S3, unofficial].
+
+### Parameters
+- `TRACE_RAY_CUDA_THREADS`: Total threads per block for ray tracing, set to 128 [S3, unofficial].
+- `WARP_SIZE`: The number of threads per warp, set to 32 [S2, unofficial].
+- `TRACE_RAY_CUDA_RAYS_PER_BLOCK`: Number of rays processed per block, calculated as `TRACE_RAY_CUDA_THREADS / WARP_SIZE` (4 rays) [S2, unofficial].
+- `grid.basis_dim`: The number of SH basis functions per color channel, determining the grouping of warps for parallel SH evaluation [S1, unofficial].
+- `opt.step_size`: The fixed step size for ray marching through the grid [S1, unofficial].
+- `opt.sigma_thresh`: The density threshold below which samples are skipped (treated as transparent) [S1, unofficial].
+- `opt.stop_thresh`: The transmission threshold below which ray marching terminates early [S1, unofficial].
+- `opt.last_sample_opaque`: Boolean flag; if true, sets `ray.world_step` to $10^9$ for the last sample to prevent attenuation [S1, unofficial].
+
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+- If `ray.tmin > ray.tmax`, the ray is outside the grid [S2, unofficial]. Output `background_brightness` if `grid.background_nlayers == 0`, else 0 [S3, unofficial]. Set `log_transmit` to 0 if `out_log_transmit` is not null [S2, unofficial].
+- Precision issues may arise from repeated floating-point additions in the ray marching loop; using `fmaf` helps maintain precision [S2, unofficial].
+- The SH basis evaluation must be synchronized across the warp before color accumulation to ensure correct reduction [S2, unofficial].
